{
  "title": "Boss: a locked-down Tasks API",
  "summary": "Evaluate policies yourself, then build an API that denies by default and checks ownership as well as roles.",
  "minutes": 30,
  "kind": "boss",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "The brief",
      "body": [
        "Authorization is more than roles. In this boss you will write a tiny policy evaluator, then an API where:",
        "",
        "- every endpoint requires a signed-in user unless it opts out (**deny by default**),",
        "- writes need a scope,",
        "- users may only see and delete **their own** tasks, while admins see everything. That last rule needs the *resource* to decide, so it lives in the endpoint, not in a policy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "A policy evaluator",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `int Evaluate(ClaimsPrincipal user, string? policy)` returning `401`, `403` or `200`:",
        "",
        "- not authenticated -> `401` (always, whatever the policy)",
        "- `policy` `null` -> `200`",
        "- `\"role:<name>\"` -> `IsInRole`",
        "- `\"scope:<name>\"` -> the space-separated `scope` claim contains it exactly",
        "- `\"claim:<type>=<value>\"` -> `user.HasClaim(type, value)`",
        "- anything else -> `403` (unknown policies deny)",
        "",
        "The tests import `System.Security.Claims`."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "int Evaluate(ClaimsPrincipal user, string? policy)",
        "{",
        "    return 200;",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "int Evaluate(ClaimsPrincipal user, string? policy)",
        "{",
        "    if (user.Identity?.IsAuthenticated != true) return 401;",
        "    if (policy is null) return 200;",
        "    if (policy.StartsWith(\"role:\")) return user.IsInRole(policy[5..]) ? 200 : 403;",
        "    if (policy.StartsWith(\"scope:\"))",
        "    {",
        "        var granted = user.FindFirst(\"scope\")?.Value.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries) ?? [];",
        "        return granted.Contains(policy[6..]) ? 200 : 403;",
        "    }",
        "    if (policy.StartsWith(\"claim:\"))",
        "    {",
        "        var pair = policy[6..].Split('=', 2);",
        "        return user.HasClaim(pair[0], pair[1]) ? 200 : 403;",
        "    }",
        "    return 403;",
        "}"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Check authentication first.",
        "`policy[5..]` after `\"role:\"`, `policy[6..]` after `\"scope:\"` and `\"claim:\"`.",
        "Split the claim part on `'='` with a limit of 2."
      ],
      "template": [
        "using System.Security.Claims;",
        "{{CODE}}",
        "var dojoAnon = new ClaimsPrincipal(new ClaimsIdentity());",
        "var dojoAda = new ClaimsPrincipal(new ClaimsIdentity([new Claim(\"sub\", \"ada\"), new Claim(\"role\", \"editor\"), new Claim(\"scope\", \"tasks:read tasks:write\"), new Claim(\"email_verified\", \"true\")], \"Bearer\", \"sub\", \"role\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"anonymous, no policy -> 401\", 401, Evaluate(dojoAnon, null));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"anonymous, role policy -> 401\", 401, Evaluate(dojoAnon, \"role:editor\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"signed in, no policy -> 200\", 200, Evaluate(dojoAda, null));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"role:editor -> 200\", 200, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"role:editor\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"role:admin -> 403\", 403, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"role:admin\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"scope:tasks:write -> 200\", 200, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"scope:tasks:write\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"scope:tasks -> 403\", 403, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"scope:tasks\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"claim:email_verified=true -> 200\", 200, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"claim:email_verified=true\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"claim:email_verified=false -> 403\", 403, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"claim:email_verified=false\"));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"unknown policy -> 403\", 403, Evaluate(dojoAda, \"magic\"));"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "framework": "web",
      "title": "Deny by default, own your data",
      "prompt": [
        "The starter has `HsBearerHandler` and `TokenValidator`. Build the API. **Run checks** starts the server and calls it.",
        "",
        "- Register the `\"Bearer\"` scheme, a **fallback policy** that requires an authenticated user, `\"Admin\"` (role `admin`) and `\"TasksWrite\"` (scope `tasks:write`).",
        "- `GET /health` -> `\"ok\"`, anonymous allowed.",
        "- `GET /tasks` -> the caller's tasks (`Owner == Identity.Name`), or all tasks for admins, ordered by id.",
        "- `POST /tasks` `{title}` (`TasksWrite`) -> `201` with `{id, title, owner}`. Ids start at 1.",
        "- `DELETE /tasks/{id}` (`TasksWrite`) -> `404` unknown, `403` not the owner and not admin, else `204`.",
        "- `GET /admin/stats` (`Admin`) -> `{count}`.",
        "",
        "Records `NewTask(string? Title)` and `TaskItem(int Id, string Title, string Owner)` are yours to add at the bottom."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Security.Claims;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Text;",
        "using System.Text.Encodings.Web;",
        "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication;",
        "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization;",
        "using Microsoft.Extensions.Options;",
        "",
        "var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);",
        "",
        "// TODO: authentication, authorization (with a deny-by-default fallback), endpoints",
        "",
        "var app = builder.Build();",
        "",
        "app.Run();",
        "",
        "class HsBearerHandler(IOptionsMonitor<AuthenticationSchemeOptions> options, ILoggerFactory logger, UrlEncoder encoder)",
        "    : AuthenticationHandler<AuthenticationSchemeOptions>(options, logger, encoder)",
        "{",
        "    protected override Task<AuthenticateResult> HandleAuthenticateAsync()",
        "    {",
        "        var header = Request.Headers.Authorization.ToString();",
        "        if (header.Length == 0) return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.NoResult());",
        "        if (!header.StartsWith(\"Bearer \", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))",
        "            return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.Fail(\"Not a bearer token.\"));",
        "",
        "        var payload = TokenValidator.ValidatePayload(header[7..].Trim(), DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeSeconds());",
        "        if (payload is null) return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.Fail(\"Invalid token.\"));",
        "",
        "        var principal = TokenValidator.ToPrincipal(payload, Scheme.Name);",
        "        return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.Success(new AuthenticationTicket(principal, Scheme.Name)));",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    protected override Task HandleChallengeAsync(AuthenticationProperties properties)",
        "    {",
        "        Response.StatusCode = 401;",
        "        Response.Headers.WWWAuthenticate = \"Bearer\";",
        "        return Task.CompletedTask;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "static class TokenValidator",
        "{",
        "    public static readonly byte[] Key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"aspnet-demo-signing-key-0123456789ab\");",
        "",
        "    // Checks alg, signature, exp (30 s skew), iss and aud. Returns the payload JSON, or null.",
        "    public static string? ValidatePayload(string token, long now)",
        "    {",
        "        var parts = token.Split('.');",
        "        if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "        try",
        "        {",
        "            using var header = JsonDocument.Parse(FromB64Url(parts[0]));",
        "            if (!header.RootElement.TryGetProperty(\"alg\", out var alg) || alg.GetString() != \"HS256\") return null;",
        "            var mac = HMACSHA256.HashData(Key, Encoding.ASCII.GetBytes(parts[0] + \".\" + parts[1]));",
        "            if (!CryptographicOperations.FixedTimeEquals(mac, FromB64Url(parts[2]))) return null;",
        "",
        "            var json = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(FromB64Url(parts[1]));",
        "            using var payload = JsonDocument.Parse(json);",
        "            var p = payload.RootElement;",
        "            if (!p.TryGetProperty(\"exp\", out var exp) || exp.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Number || now >= exp.GetInt64() + 30) return null;",
        "            if (!p.TryGetProperty(\"iss\", out var iss) || iss.GetString() != \"https://auth.dojo\") return null;",
        "            if (!p.TryGetProperty(\"aud\", out var aud) || aud.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.String || aud.GetString() != \"tasks-api\") return null;",
        "            return json;",
        "        }",
        "        catch (Exception e) when (e is FormatException or JsonException or InvalidOperationException)",
        "        {",
        "            return null;",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    static byte[] FromB64Url(string text)",
        "    {",
        "        var s = text.Replace('-', '+').Replace('_', '/');",
        "        if (s.Length % 4 == 1) throw new FormatException();",
        "        return Convert.FromBase64String(s.PadRight(s.Length + (4 - s.Length % 4) % 4, '='));",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public static ClaimsPrincipal ToPrincipal(string payloadJson, string scheme)",
        "    {",
        "        using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(payloadJson);",
        "        var claims = new List<Claim>();",
        "        foreach (var prop in doc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())",
        "        {",
        "            if (prop.Value.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)",
        "                foreach (var item in prop.Value.EnumerateArray()) claims.Add(new Claim(prop.Name, item.ToString()));",
        "            else",
        "                claims.Add(new Claim(prop.Name, prop.Value.ToString()));",
        "        }",
        "        return new ClaimsPrincipal(new ClaimsIdentity(claims, scheme, \"sub\", \"role\"));",
        "    }",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Security.Claims;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Text;",
        "using System.Text.Encodings.Web;",
        "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication;",
        "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization;",
        "using Microsoft.Extensions.Options;",
        "",
        "var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);",
        "",
        "builder.Services.AddAuthentication(\"Bearer\")",
        "    .AddScheme<AuthenticationSchemeOptions, HsBearerHandler>(\"Bearer\", null);",
        "",
        "builder.Services.AddAuthorization(options =>",
        "{",
        "    options.FallbackPolicy = new AuthorizationPolicyBuilder().RequireAuthenticatedUser().Build();",
        "    options.AddPolicy(\"Admin\", p => p.RequireRole(\"admin\"));",
        "    options.AddPolicy(\"TasksWrite\", p => p.RequireAssertion(c =>",
        "        c.User.FindFirst(\"scope\")?.Value.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries).Contains(\"tasks:write\") == true));",
        "});",
        "",
        "var tasks = new System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentDictionary<int, TaskItem>();",
        "var nextId = 0;",
        "",
        "var app = builder.Build();",
        "app.UseAuthentication();",
        "app.UseAuthorization();",
        "",
        "app.MapGet(\"/health\", () => \"ok\").AllowAnonymous();",
        "",
        "app.MapGet(\"/tasks\", (ClaimsPrincipal user) =>",
        "    tasks.Values.Where(t => t.Owner == user.Identity!.Name || user.IsInRole(\"admin\")).OrderBy(t => t.Id).ToList());",
        "",
        "app.MapPost(\"/tasks\", (NewTask body, ClaimsPrincipal user) =>",
        "{",
        "    var id = Interlocked.Increment(ref nextId);",
        "    var task = new TaskItem(id, body.Title ?? \"\", user.Identity!.Name!);",
        "    tasks[id] = task;",
        "    return Results.Created($\"/tasks/{id}\", task);",
        "}).RequireAuthorization(\"TasksWrite\");",
        "",
        "app.MapDelete(\"/tasks/{id:int}\", (int id, ClaimsPrincipal user) =>",
        "{",
        "    if (!tasks.TryGetValue(id, out var task)) return Results.NotFound();",
        "    if (task.Owner != user.Identity!.Name && !user.IsInRole(\"admin\")) return Results.StatusCode(403);",
        "    tasks.TryRemove(id, out _);",
        "    return Results.NoContent();",
        "}).RequireAuthorization(\"TasksWrite\");",
        "",
        "app.MapGet(\"/admin/stats\", () => new { count = tasks.Count }).RequireAuthorization(\"Admin\");",
        "",
        "app.Run();",
        "",
        "record NewTask(string? Title);",
        "record TaskItem(int Id, string Title, string Owner);",
        "",
        "class HsBearerHandler(IOptionsMonitor<AuthenticationSchemeOptions> options, ILoggerFactory logger, UrlEncoder encoder)",
        "    : AuthenticationHandler<AuthenticationSchemeOptions>(options, logger, encoder)",
        "{",
        "    protected override Task<AuthenticateResult> HandleAuthenticateAsync()",
        "    {",
        "        var header = Request.Headers.Authorization.ToString();",
        "        if (header.Length == 0) return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.NoResult());",
        "        if (!header.StartsWith(\"Bearer \", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))",
        "            return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.Fail(\"Not a bearer token.\"));",
        "",
        "        var payload = TokenValidator.ValidatePayload(header[7..].Trim(), DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeSeconds());",
        "        if (payload is null) return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.Fail(\"Invalid token.\"));",
        "",
        "        var principal = TokenValidator.ToPrincipal(payload, Scheme.Name);",
        "        return Task.FromResult(AuthenticateResult.Success(new AuthenticationTicket(principal, Scheme.Name)));",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    protected override Task HandleChallengeAsync(AuthenticationProperties properties)",
        "    {",
        "        Response.StatusCode = 401;",
        "        Response.Headers.WWWAuthenticate = \"Bearer\";",
        "        return Task.CompletedTask;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "static class TokenValidator",
        "{",
        "    public static readonly byte[] Key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"aspnet-demo-signing-key-0123456789ab\");",
        "",
        "    // Checks alg, signature, exp (30 s skew), iss and aud. Returns the payload JSON, or null.",
        "    public static string? ValidatePayload(string token, long now)",
        "    {",
        "        var parts = token.Split('.');",
        "        if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "        try",
        "        {",
        "            using var header = JsonDocument.Parse(FromB64Url(parts[0]));",
        "            if (!header.RootElement.TryGetProperty(\"alg\", out var alg) || alg.GetString() != \"HS256\") return null;",
        "            var mac = HMACSHA256.HashData(Key, Encoding.ASCII.GetBytes(parts[0] + \".\" + parts[1]));",
        "            if (!CryptographicOperations.FixedTimeEquals(mac, FromB64Url(parts[2]))) return null;",
        "",
        "            var json = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(FromB64Url(parts[1]));",
        "            using var payload = JsonDocument.Parse(json);",
        "            var p = payload.RootElement;",
        "            if (!p.TryGetProperty(\"exp\", out var exp) || exp.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Number || now >= exp.GetInt64() + 30) return null;",
        "            if (!p.TryGetProperty(\"iss\", out var iss) || iss.GetString() != \"https://auth.dojo\") return null;",
        "            if (!p.TryGetProperty(\"aud\", out var aud) || aud.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.String || aud.GetString() != \"tasks-api\") return null;",
        "            return json;",
        "        }",
        "        catch (Exception e) when (e is FormatException or JsonException or InvalidOperationException)",
        "        {",
        "            return null;",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    static byte[] FromB64Url(string text)",
        "    {",
        "        var s = text.Replace('-', '+').Replace('_', '/');",
        "        if (s.Length % 4 == 1) throw new FormatException();",
        "        return Convert.FromBase64String(s.PadRight(s.Length + (4 - s.Length % 4) % 4, '='));",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public static ClaimsPrincipal ToPrincipal(string payloadJson, string scheme)",
        "    {",
        "        using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(payloadJson);",
        "        var claims = new List<Claim>();",
        "        foreach (var prop in doc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())",
        "        {",
        "            if (prop.Value.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)",
        "                foreach (var item in prop.Value.EnumerateArray()) claims.Add(new Claim(prop.Name, item.ToString()));",
        "            else",
        "                claims.Add(new Claim(prop.Name, prop.Value.ToString()));",
        "        }",
        "        return new ClaimsPrincipal(new ClaimsIdentity(claims, scheme, \"sub\", \"role\"));",
        "    }",
        "}"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`options.FallbackPolicy = new AuthorizationPolicyBuilder().RequireAuthenticatedUser().Build();`",
        "Inject `ClaimsPrincipal user` into the handlers; `user.Identity!.Name` is the `sub`.",
        "Ownership is checked in the DELETE handler after loading the task: return `Results.StatusCode(403)`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "",
        "static class DojoTests",
        "{",
        "    public static async Task Run(HttpClient http)",
        "    {",
        "        var ada = DojoAuth.For(\"ada\", \"[\\\"user\\\"]\", \"tasks:read tasks:write\");",
        "        var bob = DojoAuth.For(\"bob\", \"[\\\"user\\\"]\", \"tasks:read tasks:write\");",
        "        var reader = DojoAuth.For(\"rita\", \"[\\\"user\\\"]\", \"tasks:read\");",
        "        var root = DojoAuth.For(\"root\", \"[\\\"admin\\\"]\", \"tasks:read tasks:write\");",
        "        await Dojo.TryAsync(\"Deny by default could be checked\", async () =>",
        "        {",
        "            Dojo.Eq(\"GET /health is open\", \"ok\", await DojoWeb.Text(await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Get, \"/health\", null)));",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"GET /tasks anonymously gets 401 (fallback policy)\", 401, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Get, \"/tasks\", null));",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"GET /admin/stats as a user gets 403\", 403, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Get, \"/admin/stats\", ada));",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"GET /admin/stats as admin gets 200\", 200, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Get, \"/admin/stats\", root));",
        "        });",
        "        await Dojo.TryAsync(\"Ownership could be checked\", async () =>",
        "        {",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"POST /tasks without tasks:write gets 403\", 403, await Post(http, reader, \"nope\"));",
        "            var created = await Post(http, ada, \"ada's task\");",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"POST /tasks as ada gets 201\", 201, created);",
        "            Dojo.Eq(\"the owner is ada\", \"ada\", DojoWeb.Prop(await DojoWeb.Json(created), \"owner\"));",
        "            await Post(http, bob, \"bob's task\");",
        "            var mine = await DojoWeb.Json(await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Get, \"/tasks\", ada));",
        "            Dojo.Eq(\"ada lists only her task\", \"ada's task\", mine.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array ? string.Join(\"|\", mine.EnumerateArray().Select(t => DojoWeb.Prop(t, \"title\"))) : \"(not an array)\");",
        "            var all = await DojoWeb.Json(await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Get, \"/tasks\", root));",
        "            Dojo.Eq(\"admin lists both\", 2, all.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array ? all.GetArrayLength() : -1);",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"bob can't delete ada's task (403)\", 403, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Delete, \"/tasks/1\", bob));",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"a missing task gets 404\", 404, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Delete, \"/tasks/99\", ada));",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"ada deletes her own task (204)\", 204, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Delete, \"/tasks/1\", ada));",
        "            DojoWeb.Status(\"admin deletes bob's task (204)\", 204, await DojoAuth.Send(http, HttpMethod.Delete, \"/tasks/2\", root));",
        "        });",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    static Task<HttpResponseMessage> Post(HttpClient http, string token, string title)",
        "    {",
        "        var msg = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, \"/tasks\") { Content = JsonContent.Create(new { title }) };",
        "        msg.Headers.TryAddWithoutValidation(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer \" + token);",
        "        return http.SendAsync(msg);",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "static class DojoAuth",
        "{",
        "    static string B64(byte[] d) => Convert.ToBase64String(d).TrimEnd('=').Replace('+', '-').Replace('/', '_');",
        "    static string B64(string s) => B64(System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(s));",
        "",
        "    public static string Sign(string payload, string? key = null, string header = \"{\\\"alg\\\":\\\"HS256\\\",\\\"typ\\\":\\\"JWT\\\"}\")",
        "    {",
        "        var input = B64(header) + \".\" + B64(payload);",
        "        var k = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(key ?? \"aspnet-demo-signing-key-0123456789ab\");",
        "        return input + \".\" + B64(System.Security.Cryptography.HMACSHA256.HashData(k, System.Text.Encoding.ASCII.GetBytes(input)));",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    // A valid token for tasks-api that expires in 2100.",
        "    public static string For(string sub, string roles = \"[]\", string scope = \"\", long exp = 4102444800) =>",
        "        Sign(\"{\\\"iss\\\":\\\"https://auth.dojo\\\",\\\"aud\\\":\\\"tasks-api\\\",\\\"sub\\\":\\\"\" + sub + \"\\\",\\\"role\\\":\" + roles + \",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"\" + scope + \"\\\",\\\"exp\\\":\" + exp + \"}\");",
        "",
        "    public static Task<HttpResponseMessage> Send(HttpClient http, HttpMethod method, string url, string? token, string scheme = \"Bearer\")",
        "    {",
        "        var msg = new HttpRequestMessage(method, url);",
        "        if (token is not null) msg.Headers.TryAddWithoutValidation(\"Authorization\", scheme + \" \" + token);",
        "        return http.SendAsync(msg);",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    public static string Challenge(HttpResponseMessage r) =>",
        "        r.Headers.WwwAuthenticate.Count > 0 ? string.Join(\",\", r.Headers.WwwAuthenticate) : \"\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "FallbackPolicy",
          "message": "Denies by default with a fallback policy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "framework": "web",
      "title": "The handler, from scratch",
      "prompt": [
        "Last step: the starter has the `TokenValidator` but **no handler**. Write `HsBearerHandler` yourself and wire it up, then protect `GET /me` (any user, returns `{sub}`) and `DELETE /admin/tasks/{id}` (role `admin`, returns `204`). `/public` returns `\"hello\"` openly.",
        "",
        "Your handler must answer a challenge with `401` and `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`, treat a missing header as anonymous, and treat a non-Bearer or invalid credential as a failure. **Run checks** starts the server and calls it."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Security.Claims;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Text;",
        "using System.Text.Encodings.Web;",
        "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication;",
        "using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization;",
        "using Microsoft.Extensions.Options;",
        "",
        "var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);",
        "",
        "// TODO: register a \"Bearer\" scheme using a handler you write below",
        "",
        "var app = builder.Build();",
        "",
        "app.MapGet(\"/public\", () => \"hello\");",
        "",
        "app.Run();",
        "",
        "// TODO: class HsBearerHandler",
        "",
        "static class TokenValidator",
        "{",
        "    public static readonly byte[] Key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(\"aspnet-demo-signing-key-0123456789ab\");",
        "",
        "    // Checks alg, signature, exp (30 s skew), iss and aud. Returns the payload JSON, or null.",
        "    public static string? ValidatePayload(string token, long now)",
        "    {",
        "        var parts = token.Split('.');",
        "        if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "        try",
